Since April, people have reported bookings landing on the wrong day. The export
dated 4 October records what was received and what was merged into this source ticket.

The desk marked the ticket known and claimed one parser fix would cover it. The
tenant directory and entry paths do not support that claim: the shared parser and
the booking-v3 date hint fail in different ways.

<Callout>
Closed for different reasons: engineering fixed the parser, while the hint was
closed without a fix because booking-v3 was retired.
</Callout>

The [signed review](/kb/incidents/4471-split) explains the evidence and uncertainty.
Track the [parser issue](https://github.com/mikimik01/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2)
separately from the
[form-hint issue](https://github.com/mikimik01/s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).

## Engineering update after the export

The course desk's update says #4471 closed on 5 October 2026. The parser is
**FIXED**, with `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. The hint is
**WON'T FIX**, because the booking-v3 form was retired. The parser issue is
therefore closed as completed; the hint issue is closed as not planned.

These are engineering's reported resolutions, not production changes made in
this knowledge-base repository. The counts below still describe the original
export dated 4 October.

